      'In the radio settings, with Hamlib, there is a “Use a rigctld that is already running” button for those who already have their own Hamlib started (as with oplog or WSJT-X): it picks the NET rigctl model, writes 127.0.0.1:4532 in the port (unless a network address is already there) and turns “Share with other programs” off. Then press Apply and Connect: Aurora does not open the radio’s COM port, it talks to the rigctld that is already running.',
